  "body": "## Outcome\n\nAdvance issue #16 with registration ownership and failure safeguards. This is not full resident lifecycle certification and does not install a service or birth a real organism on the creator's PC.\n\n## Changes and reasons\n\n- Refuse local/unit collisions and remove Windows task creation's forced-replacement option. A NEST must not overwrite an unrelated OS registration.\n- Preserve a pending receipt before OS changes, then mark registered only after verification. Retain failure evidence rather than guessing whether rollback is safe.\n- Rederive removal targets from the NEST and validate strict bounded receipts, expected runner bytes, current task SID/action/privilege or exact loaded unit with no drop-ins.\n- Check Linux loaded configuration before service start. Request Windows task stop before deletion; stop failure prevents deletion.\n- Keep legacy receipts readable and missing runners visible; distinguish receipt-only status from actual running-state proof.\n- Synchronize PLAN.md, coding contract, resident evidence documentation, changelog, Hermes runtime payload and seed checksums.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Local Windows suite: 188 passed, 2 explicit platform skips (real POSIX SIGTERM and unavailable symlink privilege).\n- Ruff and whitespace checks passed.\n- All seed checksums, manifest payload hashes and normalized source/runtime mirror verified.\n- New OS-fixture tests cover altered receipts, XML/owner/action drift, collisions, unsupported paths, overridden units, pending evidence, stop failure and bounded noninteractive command execution.\n- Required CI must pass before merge, including Windows/Linux Python 3.11\u20133.13, CodeQL and pinned Hermes gates.\n\n## Remaining boundaries\n\nNative task XML variants, already-stopped task behavior, actual service-manager restart/removal and interrupted-removal recovery still require disposable native certification. Preflight checks are not a transaction with the OS, a concurrent-attacker guarantee, stale-writer fencing or an atomic Heartbeat checkpoint. No automatic recovery/deletion of uncertain installations is added. Issue #16 remains open.\n",
